            <ArticleTitle>Etidocaine hydrochloride in surgical procedures: effects on postoperative analgesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>429-32, 434</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Because early research has established the prolonged duration of the effects of etidocaine, this study was performed to determine whether the long-acting local anesthetic can reduce the need for postoperative analgesics after oral surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
